tests {
  test("Status 200", function() { expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200); });
  test("success true", function() { expect(res.getBody().success).to.equal(true); });
  test("has deleted array", function() { expect(res.getBody().data.deleted).to.be.an("array"); });
}

docs {
  ## Bulk Delete Spaces Files (Superuser) — POST /uploads/spaces-files/bulk-delete

  Permanently deletes up to 200 files from DigitalOcean Spaces in one call.
  **Superuser role only** — any other authenticated role gets `403`. There is
  no trash/undo — this is a real delete against the live Space.

  Use `objectKey` values exactly as returned by `GET /uploads/spaces-files`
  (the `files[].objectKey` field).

  Deleting a file here does **not** remove any reference to its URL that may
  already be saved on an expense/visit/task-activity/etc. row in our own
  database — those rows would be left pointing at a now-missing file. Confirm
  none of the selected files are still referenced before deleting.

  A partial failure (e.g. a key that no longer exists) does not fail the
  whole batch — check `errors[]` for anything that didn't delete.

  ### Request body

  | Field      | Type     | Required | Notes                                                    |
  |------------|----------|----------|--------------------------------------------------------------|
  | objectKeys | string[] | yes      | 1–200 keys, each must start with the configured Spaces folder (e.g. `MyActivity/`) — any key outside it is rejected with `400` for the whole request |

  ### Response (200) — `data` object

  | Field           | Type     | Notes                                           |
  |-----------------|----------|---------------------------------------------------|
  | deleted         | string[] | object keys that were successfully deleted         |
  | errors          | object[] | `{ objectKey, message }` for any key that failed to delete |
}
